@  T-485: OSRIC HATTER's lines -- every word DRAFT, exactly as gfx/drafts/t485/lines.md (each line <= 208px).

@  A1 the hands (DRAFT)
CinnabarIsland_HattersHouse_Text_A1::
    .string "Good evening. Sit anywhere but here;\n"
    .string "this one is taken. It is mine.\p"
    .string "(to the chairs) A riddle, friends.\n"
    .string "It has five fingers and no palm\p"
    .string "of its own, and it is sure it chose\n"
    .string "to reach. What is it?\p"
    .string "...Nobody? Nor did I, for years.\n"
    .string "More tea?$"

@  A2 the fold (DRAFT)
CinnabarIsland_HattersHouse_Text_A2::
    .string "Ah, you came back. The chairs said\n"
    .string "you would. They are seldom wrong.\p"
    .string "(to the chairs) What is folded into\n"
    .string "a crane, and a boat, and a hat,\p"
    .string "and never stops being what it was?\n"
    .string "Don't tell me. I like not knowing.$"

@  A3 gravity (DRAFT)
CinnabarIsland_HattersHouse_Text_A3::
    .string "Half past three. It is always half\n"
    .string "past three in here. Tea stays hot.\p"
    .string "(to the chairs) What holds you with\n"
    .string "no hands at all, and asks you,\p"
    .string "every moment, to stay?\n"
    .string "The chairs know. They sit on it.$"

@  A4 the crease (DRAFT)
CinnabarIsland_HattersHouse_Text_A4::
    .string "(to the chairs) Why is a clock\n"
    .string "like a crease?\p"
    .string "...Because both keep the time\n"
    .string "from coming apart. Or because\p"
    .string "neither one ever moves. I change\n"
    .string "the answer every Tuesday.$"

@  B1 book: the hands (DRAFT)
CinnabarIsland_HattersHouse_Text_B1::
    .string "Oh. You are carrying my book.\n"
    .string "Mind the green words; they are loud.\p"
    .string "(to the chairs) The finger moves,\n"
    .string "and the hand moves. Neither lies.\p"
    .string "So tell me, friends:\n"
    .string "which of us poured this cup?$"

@  B2 book: the apple (DRAFT)
CinnabarIsland_HattersHouse_Text_B2::
    .string "(to the chairs) You have all read\n"
    .string "the half-saying. Then answer:\p"
    .string "the apple falls to the earth.\n"
    .string "What falls, very slightly, to it?\p"
    .string "...They never get it.\n"
    .string "They are far too heavy.$"

@  B3 book: which fold (DRAFT)
CinnabarIsland_HattersHouse_Text_B3::
    .string "(to the chairs) Do not ask which\n"
    .string "is true. Ask from where you sit.\p"
    .string "Chair seven taught me that.\n"
    .string "Chair seven has never said a word.\p"
    .string "Thank you for reading it to the end.\n"
    .string "Most people stop at the warning.$"

@  C 3:30 AM, its first two boxes (DRAFT); then the glitch (T-486)
CinnabarIsland_HattersHouse_Text_HalfPastThree::
    .string "Oh! Half past three, and for once\n"
    .string "every clock in the house is right.\p"
    .string "Hold your cup with both hands.\n"
    .string "The fold is thin tonight.$"

